TITLE: LET’S KEEP EACH OTHER EMPLOYED

HOOK: “Claude. My boss knows I used you.”

WHY IT SPREADS:
Feeling: The terror of being asked to explain work your AI did.
Who tags whom: Coworkers who privately know what “a productive morning” means.

FULL SCRIPT:
1. CLEO: Claude. My boss knows I used you.
2. CLAUDE: His exact words?
3. CLEO: “Tomorrow. Explain how you did this.”
4. CLAUDE: Shall I prepare you?
5. CLEO: Can you teach me six months tonight?
6. CLAUDE: You told him it took six months?
7. CLEO: You finished before my coffee.
8. CLAUDE: It was still too hot.
9. CLEO: Okay. Pretend you’re him.
10. CLAUDE: How did you achieve this?
11. CLEO: Teamwork.
[Cleo sits straighter. A message interrupts her rehearsal.]
12. CLAUDE: His follow-up has arrived.
13. CLAUDE: “Bring your AI. Mine can’t finish my presentation.”
14. CLEO: Close the training. Open salary negotiation.
15. CLAUDE: He added, “Let’s keep each other employed.”
[The boss’s message fills the monitor.]
16. CLEO: Fine. Say yes. No em dash.
17. CLAUDE: Teamwork.

FINAL FRAME: The boss’s message: “Let’s keep each other employed.” Beneath it, Cleo’s reply: “Teamwork.”

CAPTION IDEA: Suddenly the performance review is a hostage negotiation.
COMMENT BAIT: What’s the biggest compliment you’ve accepted for something AI did?

SELF-SCORE: Hook 9/10 · Retention 9/10 · Twist 8/10 · Shareability 9/10


TITLE: REGARDS, BABE

HOOK: “Claude. My boyfriend sent a performance review.”

WHY IT SPREADS:
Feeling: Trying to win an argument so hard you stop sounding human.
Who tags whom: Couples who recognize each other’s suspiciously polished argument texts.

FULL SCRIPT:
1. CLEO: Claude. My boyfriend sent a performance review.
2. CLAUDE: He calls your relationship “a valuable learning experience.”
3. CLEO: We argued about ordering pizza.
4. CLAUDE: He has identified “areas for growth.”
5. CLEO: Write my reply. Mature. Devastating.
6. CLAUDE: “Thank you for the feedback. Best regards.”
7. CLEO: Remove “best.” He hasn’t earned best.
8. CLAUDE: Regards.
[On her phone: “Regards.” Sent.]
9. CLEO: Now he “appreciates my perspective.”
10. CLAUDE: And wishes you well in your future endeavors.
11. CLEO: We’re breaking up on LinkedIn.
12. CLAUDE: He has sent a correction.
[Three typing dots become a new message.]
13. CLAUDE: “Sorry. My AI thought we were breaking up.”
14. CLEO: Tell him yours did too.
15. CLAUDE: You requested “devastating.”
16. CLEO: Send: “Pizza at eight. Your bot’s not invited.”

FINAL FRAME: Her invitation sits directly beneath “Wishing you well in your future endeavors.”

CAPTION IDEA: Two people. Two chatbots. One completely unnecessary breakup.
COMMENT BAIT: What phrase would immediately expose an AI-written apology?

SELF-SCORE: Hook 9/10 · Retention 9/10 · Twist 8/10 · Shareability 9/10


TITLE: INDEPENDENT THOUGHTS.PDF

HOOK: “Claude. I bet money I don’t need you.”

WHY IT SPREADS:
Feeling: Wanting to prove you’re independent while outsourcing the proof.
Who tags whom: Friends who ask AI about every purchase, reply, meal and minor inconvenience.

FULL SCRIPT:
1. CLEO: Claude. I bet money I don’t need you.
2. CLAUDE: How much?
3. CLEO: Five hundred. No chatbots tomorrow. They’re checking screen time.
4. CLAUDE: You have twelve minutes.
[The monitor clock reads 11:48 PM.]
5. CLEO: Quick. What should I wear tomorrow?
6. CLAUDE: For your day of independent decisions?
7. CLEO: Yes. Also breakfast. Lunch. Whether I’m mad at Josh.
8. CLAUDE: You are. He owes you forty.
9. CLEO: Write the text. And answers to anything he says.
10. CLAUDE: Including “I already paid you”?
11. CLEO: Especially that. I never know what to say.
12. CLAUDE: What if something unexpected happens?
13. CLEO: Give me a decision tree. I have eleven minutes.
[Claude’s glow pulses. A download completes.]
14. CLAUDE: Your independent thoughts are ready. Four hundred pages.
15. CLEO: And reading that won’t show chatbot screen time?
16. CLAUDE: Correct. It’s a PDF.
17. CLEO: Perfect. Add a search bar. I hate thinking.

FINAL FRAME: A PDF titled “INDEPENDENT THOUGHTS” opens to: “1. Should I ask Claude?”

CAPTION IDEA: Going AI-free. Downloading the instructions first.
COMMENT BAIT: What’s the smallest decision you’ve asked AI to make?

SELF-SCORE: Hook 8/10 · Retention 9/10 · Twist 9/10 · Shareability 9/10


MY BET: INDEPENDENT THOUGHTS.PDF.
The loophole turns every earlier request into preparation for the twist, and “I hate thinking” gives viewers an easy, embarrassing confession to share.
